{"from": "claim:ac-24-15-resurrection-hope", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:daniel-12-2", "note": "Cross-reference: 'many of those who sleep in the dust of the earth will awake' (Daniel 12:2) is the classic scriptural basis of a resurrection 'both of the just and unjust'. Biblical cross-reference, not independent evidence."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-15-resurrection-hope", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-23-08-pharisees-resurrection", "note": "Paul says his accusers 'also themselves look for' the resurrection (24:15): his confession instantiates the Pharisaic doctrine recorded by Josephus."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-21-judged-resurrection", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-23-08-pharisees-resurrection", "note": "The council dispute Paul recalls (23:6) is the same Pharisee/Sadducee resurrection doctrine."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-17-alms-collection", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:romans-15-25-26", "note": "Cross-reference: Paul's collection for Jerusalem - 'Macedonia and Achaia ... a certain contribution for the poor among the saints who are at Jerusalem'. Biblical, not independent evidence."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-17-alms-collection", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:1-corinthians-16-1-4", "note": "Cross-reference: 'concerning the collection for the saints' with letters to carry the gift to Jerusalem. Biblical, not independent evidence."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-06-temple-profane-charge", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-21-28-accusation", "note": "The same charge Paul 'tries to profane the temple', made in a Roman court at Caesarea (24:6) after the mob accusation in Jerusalem (21:28); different occasions, same accusation."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-06-temple-profane-charge", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-21-28-gentile-exclusion", "note": "The gravity of the profanation charge rests on the temple's Gentile-exclusion custom (attested by the Temple Warning inscription in data/acts/21)."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-18-purified-temple", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-21-26-purification-temple", "note": "The same purification-rite setting Paul refers back to; Acts 24:18 recaps 21:26."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-05-impostors-felix-era", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-21-38-egyptian-4000", "note": "The Egyptian impostor the tribune names (21:38) is the same figure Josephus places under Felix; Acts 24:5's 'insurrections among all the Jews' belongs to this epidemic."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-05-insurrection-charge", "type": "related_to", "to": "text:josephus-ant-20-theudas", "note": "Lead from ch 7: Josephus's Theudas (Ant. 20.97-98, c. 44-46) is one of the impostor-seditions of the decade before Felix; context for the 'instigator of insurrections among all the Jews throughout the world' charge."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-05-insurrection-charge", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-24-05-impostors-felix-era", "note": "The charge presupposes the seditious-impostor epidemic the context claim records."}
{"from": "claim:ac-24-20-council-hearing", "type": "related_to", "to": "claim:ac-24-21-judged-resurrection", "note": "Both are Paul's recollection of the Sanhedrin hearing of Acts 23."}
