{"from": "text:josephus-ant-20-137-144", "type": "attests", "to": "claim:ac-24-24-drusilla-person", "grade": "A", "note": "Josephus, Ant. 20.141-144: Agrippa gave his sister Drusilla to Azizus of Emesa 'upon his consent to be circumcised'; while Felix was procurator of Judea she was 'prevailed upon to transgress the laws of her forefathers, and to marry Felix' - grade A for the person and marriage (split from claim:ac-24-24-drusilla-jewess per the architect's titles/offices ruling)."}
{"from": "text:tacitus-histories-5-9", "type": "complicates", "to": "claim:ac-24-24-drusilla-person", "note": "Tacitus calls Drusilla 'the granddaughter of Antony and Cleopatra' and Felix 'the grandson-in-law' of Antony (so a pagan princess) - a different identification from Josephus's Jewish Agrippid princess, and contrary to Luke's 'a Jewess'. Same tension as on claim:ac-24-24-drusilla-jewess."}
{"from": "passage:ac-24-24", "type": "asserts", "to": "claim:ac-24-24-drusilla-person", "note": "Acts 24:24 names 'Drusilla his wife, which was a Jewess'; the hearing event is claim:ac-24-24-drusilla-jewess."}
